@lang en
IMPORT `bm-ear-general-conditions`

-- Bao Minh erection all risks rules: the duties that have a deadline or a sequence, as
-- regulative rules. The provisions are quoted where they are first encoded
-- (bm-ear-general-conditions.l4, bm-ear-part2-third-party.l4); this module cites them.
--
-- THE CLOCK. Every rule here counts CALENDAR DAYS on the trace's timeline. For General
-- Condition 5, day 0 is the day of the occurrence, and the act "give notice" is stamped on
-- the day Bao Minh RECEIVED it (src:110). For General Condition 7, day 0 is the day the
-- written request was sent, and the one-month window is converted to days from that date.
--
-- WHAT THESE RULES DO NOT DO. A trace's outcome cannot flow back into a rule. The cover
-- and amount rules read compliance from the claim file (`the duties not complied with`, the
-- date notice was received); these rules show the sequence and its deadlines.

§ `Duties with a deadline or a sequence`

§§ `General Condition 5 — notice, inspection and repair`

-- Notice must reach Bao Minh within 14 days of the occurrence, or Bao Minh is not liable
-- (src:109-111). The duty itself is "immediately" (src:94), which has no number, so the
-- rule's only deadline is the 14-day bar, and missing it is reported as the loss of cover.
-- After notice: minor damage may be repaired at once; otherwise Bao Minh may inspect, and
-- once it has, or a reasonable time has passed without inspection, the Insured may repair
-- (src:113-117). "A reasonable time" is not a number the document gives: the caller
-- supplies the time found reasonable, in days (Finding 12).
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5 (src:91-95, 109-117)
GIVEN `the damage is minor`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable time for inspection, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 5: notice, then inspection, then repair` `the damage is minor` `a reasonable time for inspection, in days` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Insured`
    MUST   `give notice of the occurrence`
    WITHIN `the days General Condition 5 allows for Bao Minh to receive notice`
    HENCE  `General Condition 5: after notice` `the damage is minor` `a reasonable time for inspection, in days`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured`
           BECAUSE "General Condition 5: Bao Minh received no notice within 14 days of the occurrence, and is not liable for the loss"

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5 (src:113-117)
GIVEN `the damage is minor`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable time for inspection, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 5: after notice` `the damage is minor` `a reasonable time for inspection, in days` MEANS
    IF   `the damage is minor`
    THEN PARTY `the Insured` MAY `repair or replace the damaged item`
    ELSE PARTY  `Bao Minh`
         MAY    `inspect the loss`
         WITHIN `a reasonable time for inspection, in days`
         HENCE  (PARTY `the Insured` MAY `repair or replace the damaged item`)
         LEST   (PARTY `the Insured` MAY `repair or replace the damaged item`)

-- (e) In case of theft, the Insured must inform the police. No time is stated (src:105),
-- so the duty carries no WITHIN.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5(e) (src:105)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 5(e): inform the police of a theft` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `inform the police of the theft`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `General Condition 4(b) — material change`

-- The Insured must notify a material change "immediately" by telegram and in writing
-- (src:81-82); no number, so no WITHIN. It must not make or admit a material change that
-- increases the risk without Bao Minh's written approval (src:87-89); no period, so the
-- prohibition lasts for the life of the policy.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 4(b) (src:81-85)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 4(b): notify a material change` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `notify Bao Minh of a material change, by telegram and in writing`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 4(b), last paragraph (src:87-89)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 4(b): no material change increasing the risk without written approval` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    SHANT `make or admit a material change that increases the risk` `approved` PROVIDED NOT `approved`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured`
          BECAUSE "General Condition 4(b): the Insured made or admitted a material change increasing the risk without Bao Minh's written approval"

§§ `General Condition 7 — appointing arbitrators`

-- Where the parties cannot agree on one arbitrator, each appoints one in writing within
-- one month after the other sends it a written request (src:133-136). The document states
-- no consequence of a failure to appoint, and no one appoints in default (Finding 7); the
-- breach below is a breach with nothing attached to it.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 7 (src:131-136)
GIVEN `the day the request was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`General Condition 7: the days allowed to appoint after a request sent on` `the day the request was sent` MEANS
        Day (`General Condition 7: the last day to appoint an arbitrator after a written request sent on` `the day the request was sent`)
    MINUS Day `the day the request was sent`

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 7 (src:131-136)
GIVEN `the party asked`               IS A `A party to the policy`
      `the day the request was sent`  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`General Condition 7: the party asked,` `the party asked` `, must appoint an arbitrator after a request sent on` `the day the request was sent` MEANS
    PARTY  `the party asked`
    MUST   `appoint an arbitrator in writing`
    WITHIN `General Condition 7: the days allowed to appoint after a request sent on` `the day the request was sent`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the party asked`
           BECAUSE "General Condition 7: no arbitrator was appointed in writing within one month of the written request; the policy states no consequence"

§§ `Part II conditions 1 and 2`

-- Condition 1: no admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity without Bao Minh's
-- written consent; no period, so for the life of the claim. Bao Minh MAY take over the
-- defence or settlement (src:301-308).
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, Part II condition 1 (src:301-303)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Part II condition 1: no admission without written consent` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    SHANT `make an admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity` `consented` PROVIDED NOT `consented`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured`
          BECAUSE "Part II condition 1: the Insured made an admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity without Bao Minh's written consent"

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, Part II condition 1 (src:303-307)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Part II condition 1: Bao Minh may take over the defence or settlement` MEANS
    PARTY `Bao Minh`
    MAY   `take over the defence or settlement of the claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Condition 2: Bao Minh MAY pay the limit (less sums already paid) or a lesser settlement
-- sum, after which it is not liable for the occurrence under Part II (src:310-314).
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, Part II condition 2 (src:310-314)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Part II condition 2: Bao Minh may pay the limit or a settlement sum` MEANS
    PARTY `Bao Minh`
    MAY   `pay the limit of indemnity less sums already paid, or a lesser sum for which the claims can be settled`
    HENCE FULFILLED
